:        self.highlighter = highlighter or ReprHighlighter()\nrich/_inspect.py:7:from .highlighter import ReprHighlighter\nrich/_inspect.py:51:        self.highlighter = ReprHighlighter()\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
